# Landing page

## Deploy

- Root for Vercel: `landing/` (see `landing/vercel.json`, `landing/README.md`)
- Static HTML/CSS/JS — no frontend build step
- Local preview: `npm run landing` or `python -m http.server 4000 --directory landing`

## Key files

- `landing/index.html` — hero, waitlist, `#demo` interactive section
- `landing/demo.js` — IIFE with dummy data (`STATS`, `SPOTLIGHT_GAMES`); mirrors app UX, no app imports
- `landing/demo.css` — demo dashboard chrome
- `landing/main.js` — waitlist POST to `/api/subscribe`
- `landing/free-claims.json` — built by `build_free_claims.py` at repo root

## Serverless

- `landing/api/subscribe.js` — waitlist (Resend + optional Supabase)
- `landing/api/report.js` — opt-in bug reports from local app

## Keep in sync

See **AGENTS.md hard rule 6** for the canonical full sync-pair list. Landing-specific:

- `landing/marquee-speed.js` ↔ `js/marquee-speed.js` (duplicate IIFE vs ESM)
- Sample covers: `landing/assets/sample/*.{webp,png}` (fictional games)
- Demo stats in `demo.js` are independent from app state — update both if changing marketing numbers

## Copy conventions

- **No em dashes or AI tells in marketing copy.** Never use `—` (em dash, U+2014) in any front-facing string in `landing/` (hero, demo text, `sponsors.json`, email copy in `api/subscribe.js`). Use a spaced hyphen (` - `) or rephrase. Also avoid LLM-flavored marketing (contrast frames, hype verbs, empty intensifiers, abstract positioning, verbatim claim repetition across sections). Code comments are exempt. See AGENTS.md hard rule 8.
